# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mountain-Able client — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development. `.env` is git-ignored.
#
# On Vercel, set this in Project Settings → Environment Variables instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the API, INCLUDING the /api path segment.
#
# Vite inlines `VITE_*` variables into the bundle **at build time**, not at run
# time. Two consequences worth knowing before deploying:
#
#   1. Changing this on Vercel requires a redeploy to take effect. Editing the
#      variable alone changes nothing about the site already being served.
#   2. The value is public. It ends up in the JavaScript any visitor can read,
#      so never put a secret in a VITE_ variable.
#
# Local development (the API running on your machine):
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api

# Production example — the Render service URL with /api appended:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://mountain-able-api.onrender.com/api
#
# The API origin is also used to resolve locally-stored upload paths
# (`/uploads/...`) into absolute URLs. Images served from Cloudinary are already
# absolute and are passed through untouched, so this stays correct either way.
